Depending on width_sel input one of them is selected. (say 01 hence, 16 mode)
I have used the maximum value in such a way that only certain no of loops are executed and others are in parallel.
[For example, in 16 mode, the max value of i is 8 (actually 7) so 128 bits is divided into 8 parts and 16 bits are added at once]

At the end of each loop the index is increased so that it reaches the 1+ the highest index of previous loop.

Also at the end the saturating add and sub have the numbers locked between 0 and max_value(which also depends on width_sel).
